WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.697
This query converts numeric quality scores into broad bands and counts customers in each band.

00:00:05.697 --> 00:00:08.792
A summary like this can help prioritize review.

00:00:08.792 --> 00:00:12.032
But the band does not replace the underlying dimensions.

00:00:12.032 --> 00:00:19.197
If a row has a low score, you should still be able to explain whether the problem is missingness,

00:00:19.197 --> 00:00:21.682
invalid contact data, timeliness, or something else.

00:00:21.682 --> 00:00:26.337
Validation is rule-based detection, not automatic correction.

00:00:26.337 --> 00:00:32.832
A failed email-shape check tells you that a record deserves attention; it does not tell you the correct email.

00:00:32.832 --> 00:00:39.325
Treat quality flags as evidence that can drive quarantine, review, or a documented repair process.
